1
00:00:01,440 --> 00:00:04,320
All right. We're about to enter the High NA lab.
好的。我们即将进入高数值孔径实验室。

2
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:09,160
Behind this highly secured door in an ASML cleanroom.
在阿斯麦洁净室的一扇高度安保的门后。

3
00:00:09,160 --> 00:00:11,880
There's a giant $400 million machine.
有一台价值4亿美元的巨型机器。

4
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:14,120
It's bigger than a double-decker bus.
它比双层巴士还要大。

5
00:00:14,440 --> 00:00:17,520
Made with such closely protected technical specificity.
采用极其严密保护的技术细节制造。

6
00:00:17,560 --> 00:00:22,880
Very complex. The most advanced machine tool in history.
非常复杂，是历史上最先进的机床。

7
00:00:22,880 --> 00:00:26,480
That no filming's ever been allowed, even by ASML's own team.
甚至阿斯麦自己的团队也从未被允许拍摄。

8
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:28,840
Until we flew across the world to see it.
直到我们飞越全球前来亲眼见证。

9
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:36,320
We're here at ASML's headquarters in the Netherlands, where 100% of the world's extreme ultraviolet lithography machines are made,
我们现在位于阿斯麦位于荷兰的总部，全球100%的极紫外光刻机都在这里制造，

10
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:39,440
and now the next generation machines called High NA.
以及下一代被称为高数值孔径的机器。

11
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:46,800
We had to wear these bunny suits to protect these extremely precise machines from getting contaminated by our own hair and skin cells.
我们必须穿上这种兔形服，以防止我们自身的头发和皮肤细胞污染这些极其精密的机器。

12
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:49,120
This is high numerical aperture.
这就是高数值孔径。

13
00:00:49,160 --> 00:00:57,840
High NA, the new generation of EUV machines, the only machines in the world capable of printing nanoscopic blueprints onto the most advanced chips.
高数值孔径（High NA）是新一代极紫外光刻机，目前全球唯一能够将纳米级蓝图印刷到最先进芯片上的设备。

14
00:00:58,120 --> 00:01:01,600
Nvidia, Apple, Taiwan Semiconductor, Samsung, Intel.
英伟达、苹果、台积电、三星、英特尔。

15
00:01:01,640 --> 00:01:04,330
None of their advanced chips can be made without EUV.
没有极紫外光刻技术，这些先进芯片都无法制造。

16
00:01:04,450 --> 00:01:07,930
And this company has that market completely cornered.
而这家公司已完全垄断了这一市场。

17
00:01:08,490 --> 00:01:11,170
The first High NA machine was installed in the U.S.
第一台高数值孔径光刻机已在美国安装。

18
00:01:11,210 --> 00:01:14,570
at Intel's Oregon chip fabrication plant, or Fab, last year.
安装在英特尔位于俄勒冈州的芯片制造厂（晶圆厂）。

19
00:01:14,810 --> 00:01:16,810
Only five have ever been shipped.
全球至今仅交付了五台。

20
00:01:16,850 --> 00:01:21,490
Indeed, the machine is so big you can't ship them in ones, so we break them into parts.
这台设备实在太大，无法整机运输，因此我们必须将其拆分成部件运输。

21
00:01:21,530 --> 00:01:29,010
Now they're being ramped up to make millions of chips on the factory floors of the few companies that can afford them Intel, TSMC and Samsung.
如今它们正被逐步投入使用，为少数能负担得起的公司——英特尔、台积电和三星——的工厂生产数百万颗芯片。

22
00:01:29,250 --> 00:01:36,610
ASML says eventually China will be used by all its EUV customers. Other advanced chipmakers like Micron, SK Hynix and Rapidus.
阿斯麦表示，最终中国也将成为其所有极紫外光刻机客户的使用对象，包括其他先进芯片制造商如美光、SK 海力士和 Rapidus。

23
00:01:36,930 --> 00:01:40,410
Without EUV, without very advanced logic manufacturing.
没有极紫外光刻技术，没有高度先进的逻辑制造工艺。

24
00:01:40,450 --> 00:01:42,250
Most of the AI cannot happen.
大多数人工智能技术将无法实现。

25
00:01:42,530 --> 00:01:49,370
CNBC went from ASML's labs in California all the way to its Veldhoven, Netherlands, headquarters to bring you this never-before-seen look at
CNBC 从阿斯麦位于加州的实验室一路来到位于荷兰费尔德霍芬的总部，为您呈现这一前所未见的镜头，

26
00:01:49,370 --> 00:01:56,810
the world's most advanced chipmaking machine and to ask its makers exactly how it works and what could go wrong, amidst Trump's tariffs,
展示世界上最先进的芯片制造设备，并向其制造商询问该设备的工作原理以及可能出现的问题，背景是特朗普的关税，

27
00:01:56,810 --> 00:02:14,620
export controls and a new training facility coming to the Suited U.S.
出口管制以及一座即将落户美国的全新培训设施。

28
00:02:14,620 --> 00:02:16,060
up and throuhj an air shower.
经过一个气淋浴间。

29
00:02:16,100 --> 00:02:21,700
It's basically to blow off all the contamination from your suit and your clothes.
主要是吹掉你服装和防护服上的所有污染物。

30
00:02:22,940 --> 00:02:26,900
Down several long hallways where humongous parts are being meticulously moved.
穿过几条长长的走廊，巨大的部件正被仔细移动。

31
00:02:27,180 --> 00:02:29,780
How many people would you say are working here? 24 /7 .
您觉得这里有多少人在工作？全天候 24/7。

32
00:02:30,180 --> 00:02:33,820
Inside the EUV factory alone, it's like 2,000 people.
仅在 EUV 工厂内部，人数就达到约 2000 人。

33
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:35,580
It's a 24 /7 operation.
这是一个全天候 24/7 的运作。

34
00:02:36,340 --> 00:02:42,500
Assia Haddou took us to the restricted lab space where 40 years of ASML's technology research all comes together.
阿西娅·哈杜带我们进入了受限制的实验室区域，这里汇聚了阿斯麦 40 年来的技术研究成果。

35
00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:47,140
It takes approximately a year and a half to create this system.
制造这套系统大约需要一年半时间。

36
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:51,140
Haddou leads the team that tests and qualifies the High NA machines here.
哈杜负责领导这里测试和认证 High NA 设备的团队。

37
00:02:51,180 --> 00:02:52,580
It still does blow my mind.
这仍然让我感到震惊。

38
00:02:52,620 --> 00:02:56,100
I think even if you learn more about it, it blows your mind even more.
我认为即使你了解更多，它仍然会让你更加震惊。

39
00:02:56,580 --> 00:03:04,780
The big machine at the end of the day is used to transfer a pattern, which we store on a mask onto a wafer, and then the end of the day,
最终，这台大型机器用于将图案从掩模转移到晶圆上，到了最后，

40
00:03:04,780 --> 00:03:09,710
you cut them in pieces, you package them, and then you end up in your phone.
你把它们切割成小块，进行封装，最后就到了你的手机里。

41
00:03:11,270 --> 00:03:21,270
Jos Benschop joined Dutch electronics giant Philips in 1984. Two weeks later, ASML was founded as a subsidiary, conducting research out of a leaky shed nearby in Eindhoven.
乔斯·本肖普于1984年加入荷兰电子巨头飞利浦，两周后，阿斯麦作为其子公司成立，研究工作在埃因霍温附近一间漏雨的棚屋里展开。

42
00:03:21,550 --> 00:03:29,430
It broke off from Philips with an IPO in 1995, and two years later, Benschop helped spearhead ASML's first foray into EUV.
1995年，它从飞利浦分拆并上市，两年后，本肖普帮助主导了阿斯麦首次进军极紫外光刻（EUV）的行动。

43
00:03:29,760 --> 00:03:34,470
Three or four years later, we had enough confidence to put all our eggs in one basket called EUV.
三到四年之后，我们有足够的信心，把所有赌注都押在了名为EUV的单一技术上。

44
00:03:34,590 --> 00:03:37,150
With hindsight, we can say we placed the right bet.
从 hindsight 来看，我们可以说押对了。

45
00:03:37,710 --> 00:03:42,390
On a yearly basis, I think we file several hundreds of patents on EUV.
每年，我们大约会提交数百项关于EUV的专利。

46
00:03:42,950 --> 00:03:48,430
Christophe Fouquet began as CEO just over a year ago, but he's been with ASML more than 17 years.
傅恪礼一年前才开始担任首席执行官，但他已在阿斯麦工作超过17年。

47
00:03:48,590 --> 00:03:49,670
We barely made it.
我们几乎没能成功。

48
00:03:49,710 --> 00:03:51,950
I think sometimes people forget that.
我觉得有时候人们会忘记这一点。

49
00:03:51,950 --> 00:03:55,990
But EUV took us practically more than 20 years.
但极紫外光刻技术几乎耗费了我们超过20年的时间。

50
00:03:56,030 --> 00:04:04,030
I would say it's been a very risky investment because when we started, well, there was no guarantee the technology would work.
我认为这是一次非常冒险的投资，因为当初开始时，这项技术能否成功尚无保障。

51
00:04:04,790 --> 00:04:10,600
By 2018, ASML had shown that EUV was possible, and it's the same process used in High NA.
到2018年，阿斯麦已经证明了极紫外光刻是可行的，这一技术同样应用于高数值孔径。

52
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:12,080
Here's how it works.
这就是它的运作原理。

53
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:20,680
Chips are built in a grid formation on thinly sliced wafers of silicon, each with up to 100 thin layers that make up billions of transistors that determine what the chips can do.
芯片在薄切的硅晶圆上以网格形式制造，每片晶圆最多可包含100层薄层，这些层共同构成数十亿个晶体管，决定了芯片的功能。

54
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:23,240
These layers are printed using lithography,
这些层通过光刻技术印刷。

55
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:30,000
extremely precise rays of light projected through a mask of the chip design until they hit the surface of the wafer that's been coated with photoresist
极其精确的光线通过芯片设计的掩模投射，最终照射到涂有光刻胶的晶圆表面。

56
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:39,240
chemicals. ASML's older generation DUV machines, which it still makes, use rays of deep ultraviolet light with a wavelength of 193 nanometers.
阿斯麦的旧一代深紫外光刻机仍在生产，使用波长为193纳米的深紫外光。

57
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:42,560
Nikon and Canon in Japan are still competitors in DUV,
日本的尼康和佳能仍是深紫外光刻领域的竞争对手。

58
00:04:42,960 --> 00:04:51,120
but ASML's real breakthrough came with that bold bet on a technology many thought was impossible using even shorter wavelength extreme ultraviolet light,
但阿斯麦真正的突破来自于大胆押注一种曾被许多人认为不可能实现的技术——使用更短波长的极紫外光。

59
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:54,520
EUV, something that to this day no other company does.
这是至今为止，没有任何其他公司能做到的技术。

60
00:04:54,760 --> 00:05:04,440
A few more people tried for many years, but the size of the investment, the commitment you have to have, I think, discouraged quite a few people.
也曾有少数人多年尝试，但投资规模巨大，所需投入的承诺程度极高，我认为这吓退了相当多的人。

61
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:08,940
Transistors have gotten so small, down to 10,000 times thinner than a human hair,
晶体管已经小到只有人类发丝厚度的万分之一，

62
00:05:08,940 --> 00:05:13,660
that ASML decided to create its own source of smaller, more precise EUV light.
因此阿斯麦决定开发自己的更小、更精确的极紫外光光源。

63
00:05:13,660 --> 00:05:19,260
At a wavelength of 13.5 nanometers, it's the width of just five DNA strands laid side by side.
波长为13.5纳米，仅相当于五条DNA链并排的宽度。

64
00:05:19,580 --> 00:05:25,940
So small that it gets absorbed by almost everything. And that's why this whole system needs to be in a vacuum.
小到几乎会被所有物质吸收，这也是整个系统必须处于真空环境的原因。

65
00:05:26,420 --> 00:05:33,380
This tiny thread may look like the strand of a spider web, but it's actually molten tin being shot out at 50,000 droplets a second.
这根细丝看起来像蜘蛛网的丝线，但实际上却是以每秒5万滴的速度喷射出的熔融锡。

66
00:05:33,660 --> 00:05:39,060
The tin droplets are vaporized with a laser, and those tiny explosions are what emit photons of EUV light.
锡滴被激光汽化，这些微小的爆炸产生了极紫外光子。

67
00:05:41,380 --> 00:05:43,020
This is called a CO2 laser.
这被称为二氧化碳激光器。

68
00:05:43,060 --> 00:05:45,140
It's been used in the car industry for many years.
它已在汽车行业使用多年。

69
00:05:45,140 --> 00:05:47,260
They would cut through steel with one of these.
他们曾用这种设备切割钢板。

70
00:05:47,540 --> 00:05:53,940
We use four of them to shoot at one of these tiny tin droplets to generate a plasma, which is hotter than the sun.
我们使用四台这样的激光器同时轰击一个微小的锡滴，产生温度超过太阳的等离子体。

71
00:05:54,460 --> 00:06:02,540
That plasma generates EUV, and that EUV is captured by this collector mirror that comes from Carl Zeiss and brings the light into our scanner.
这个等离子体发出极紫外光，由卡尔蔡司提供的收集镜捕捉，并将光线导入我们的光刻机。

72
00:06:03,180 --> 00:06:07,340
The light bounces off of mirrors that aim it through the lens, much like how a camera works.
光线通过镜面反射并聚焦到镜头，就像相机的工作原理一样。

73
00:06:07,340 --> 00:06:10,110
But because EUV gets absorbed by typical mirrors.
但因为极紫外光会被普通镜子吸收。

74
00:06:10,110 --> 00:06:16,430
German optics company Zeiss made specific mirrors just for ASML that are the flattest man made surfaces in the world.
德国光学公司蔡司为阿斯麦专门制造了镜片，其表面是目前世界上最为平坦的人造表面。

75
00:06:16,630 --> 00:06:23,350
And then the light is emitted through the projection optics onto the wafer, which is about here.
然后光线通过投影光学系统投射到晶圆上，位置大约在这里。

76
00:06:23,350 --> 00:06:25,150
So this is the wafer table.
这就是晶圆台。

77
00:06:26,190 --> 00:06:30,710
When the EUV finally hits photoresist chemicals on the surface of the silicon wafer,
当极紫外光最终照射到硅晶圆表面的光刻胶化学物质上时，

78
00:06:30,710 --> 00:06:35,470
it prints the minuscule blueprint that makes up the chip. The aim needs to be so precise,
它会打印出构成芯片的微小蓝图。目标必须如此精准，

79
00:06:35,510 --> 00:06:40,190
TSMC says it's equivalent to shining a laser from the moon to hit a coin on the Earth.
台积电表示，这相当于从月球发射一束激光，精准击中地球上的一枚硬币。

80
00:06:40,630 --> 00:06:48,710
EUV made up less than 8% of ASML's total number of machines sold in 2024: 44 EUV machines versus 374
2024年，极紫外光刻机占阿斯麦总出货量不到8%：共44台极紫外光刻机，对比374台其他机型。

81
00:06:48,710 --> 00:06:56,830
cheaper DUV machines, but with a price tag of $220 million. EUV made up 38% of ASML's system sales revenue.
更便宜的DUV设备，但价格高达2.2亿美元。EUV占阿斯麦系统销售收入的38%。

82
00:06:57,230 --> 00:07:01,830
But a cost of the chips the tool is going to create is going down.
但芯片工具所带来的成本正在下降。

83
00:07:02,070 --> 00:07:07,710
Because yo u're t he o nly c ompany in the world that makes these m achines, w hat's stopping you from setting the price even higher?
你们是全球唯一生产这些机器的公司，为什么不能把价格定得更高呢？

84
00:07:08,110 --> 00:07:13,760
Well, what stops us is Moore's Law says that we need to continue to drive costs down.
实际上，阻碍我们的原因是摩尔定律要求我们必须持续降低成本。

85
00:07:14,280 --> 00:07:20,040
This allows you to go to the next node and then the next node, and then again the next node.
这样你就可以前往下一个节点，然后是下一个节点，再然后是下一个节点。

86
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:23,280
If this was to stop, then everyone gets stuck.
如果这个过程停止，那么所有人都会卡住。

87
00:07:28,640 --> 00:07:33,960
ASML began developing its latest $400 million High NA machines around 2016.
阿斯麦大约在2016年开始研发其最新的4亿美元高数值孔径设备。

88
00:07:34,320 --> 00:07:38,920
Inside, all the same processes still happen with the same EUV light source.
内部，所有流程仍然使用相同的极紫外光源进行。

89
00:07:38,920 --> 00:07:40,800
But there's one key difference.
但有一个关键区别。

90
00:07:40,840 --> 00:07:43,920
We increase the aperture of the opening angle of the lens.
我们增大了镜头开口的孔径角。

91
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:48,480
High NA stands for high numerical aperture, meaning it has a larger lens opening,
高数值孔径指的是更大的镜头开口，

92
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:55,560
increasing the angle at which the light is captured by the mirrors. More light coming in from steeper angles allows High NA machines to capture
从而增加了镜面捕捉光线的角度。从更陡的角度进入更多的光线，使高数值孔径设备能够捕捉

93
00:07:55,560 --> 00:08:00,760
increasingly small designs on chip masks, so they can be projected in one exposure step,
芯片光罩上越来越小的设计，从而实现一次曝光步骤即可投射，

94
00:08:00,760 --> 00:08:08,280
whereas original lower NA machines reach higher resolution to project these tiny designs using multiple exposures through multiple masks.
而原始的低数值孔径设备则需通过多个光罩进行多次曝光，才能实现这些微小设计的高分辨率投射。

95
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:12,170
One become two, then two become three, three become four.
一变成二，然后二变成三，三变成四。

96
00:08:12,850 --> 00:08:17,090
And when the number increases, it gets very complex process wise.
当数量增加时，其工艺复杂度会急剧上升。

97
00:08:17,370 --> 00:08:18,730
And the yield goes down.
而良率会下降。

98
00:08:18,970 --> 00:08:25,290
But with a higher NA, resolution improves and the small designs can be printed with fewer masks, saving time and money.
但数值孔径越高，分辨率就越好，小尺寸设计可以用更少的光罩完成，节省时间和成本。

99
00:08:25,690 --> 00:08:28,970
The larger the number, the smaller the thing you can print.
数值越大，能打印的东西就越小。

100
00:08:29,170 --> 00:08:33,490
But this higher NA also comes with a much higher price tag for one main reason.
但这个更高的数值孔径也带来了一个主要问题，就是价格大幅上涨。

101
00:08:33,690 --> 00:08:40,250
The higher the NA of an optic, the bigger the mirror you have to use, and therefore the bigger the system.
光学系统的数值孔径越高，所需的镜面就越大，因此整个系统也越大。

102
00:08:40,290 --> 00:08:43,170
These machines also take up a huge amount of power.
这些机器还需要消耗巨大的电力。

103
00:08:43,450 --> 00:08:45,730
How much power do these machines take?
这些机器耗电多少？

104
00:08:46,370 --> 00:08:47,650
I think they take too much.
我认为它们耗电太多了。

105
00:08:47,650 --> 00:08:56,850
If we don't improve the power efficiency of our AI chips over time, the training of the models
如果我们不能随着时间推移提升 AI 芯片的能效，

106
00:08:56,850 --> 00:09:02,930
could consume the entire worldwide energy, and that could happen around 2035.
模型的训练可能会消耗掉全球所有的能源，这种情况可能在 2035 年左右发生。

107
00:09:02,970 --> 00:09:11,970
Since the moment we started EUV, 2018, we have reduced the power the energy needed per wafer exposure by more than 60%.
自从我们开始使用 EUV 以来，即 2018 年起，每片晶圆曝光所需的能耗已降低超过 60%。

108
00:09:12,420 --> 00:09:19,620
ASML says its machines print about 200 wafers per hour, 24/7, 365. The goal is several hundred per hour.
阿斯麦表示，其机器可实现每小时 200 片晶圆的连续生产，全年无休。目标是每小时数百片。

109
00:09:19,900 --> 00:09:23,300
You can print at the end of the day, millions of these wafers per year.
你可以在一天结束时，每年生产数百万片这样的晶圆。

110
00:09:23,580 --> 00:09:32,780
At a conference in February, Intel said it started making chips with High NA using it for some 30,000 wafers so far, and that it's about twice as reliable as previous models.
在二月份的一场会议上，英特尔表示，它已开始使用 High NA 技术制造芯片，迄今已用于约3万片晶圆，且其可靠性比之前模型高出约一倍。

111
00:09:33,020 --> 00:09:36,860
And Samsung said High NA could reduce its cycle time by 60%.
三星表示，High NA 可将其生产周期缩短60%。

112
00:09:37,420 --> 00:09:38,980
High NA means two things.
High NA 意味着两件事。

113
00:09:38,980 --> 00:09:40,340
First and foremost, shrink.
首要的是缩小尺寸。

114
00:09:40,340 --> 00:09:42,860
So there's more devices on a single wafer.
这样单片晶圆上就能集成更多器件。

115
00:09:43,180 --> 00:09:48,740
And secondly, by avoiding multiple patterning, you can make them faster and you can make them with higher yield.
其次，通过避免多重曝光，可以制造得更快，同时提高良率。

116
00:09:51,700 --> 00:09:56,860
In reality, every chip is made using multiple different lithography techniques at different resolutions.
实际上，每颗芯片都是在不同分辨率下，使用多种不同的光刻技术制造的。

117
00:09:56,860 --> 00:10:01,220
Every chip consists out of like 100 different layers.
每颗芯片由大约100个不同层构成。

118
00:10:01,220 --> 00:10:07,460
Most of the layers are actually made with deep UV, which is a much smaller system.
其中大多数层实际上都是用深紫外光刻技术制造的，这是一种更小的系统。

119
00:10:07,980 --> 00:10:14,750
Legacy DUV machines sell for less 5$ million to $90 million, but still make up over half of ASML's sales.
传统 DUV 设备售价低于500万美元至900万美元，但仍然占阿斯麦销售额的一半以上。

120
00:10:14,790 --> 00:10:16,670
The older machines are in high demand.
旧款设备需求旺盛。

121
00:10:17,030 --> 00:10:26,590
Many of the chips we use in our daily life do not require DEUV. If you press the button to open the window in your car, unlikely an EUV-based chip is needed.
我们日常生活中使用的许多芯片并不需要极紫外光刻技术。如果你按下汽车窗户的开关按钮，几乎不可能需要用到基于极紫外光刻的芯片。

122
00:10:26,950 --> 00:10:30,710
Turns out ASML sells a lot of its legacy machines to China, although U.S.
结果发现，尽管美国实施了出口管制，阿斯麦仍向中国出售了大量旧款设备。

123
00:10:30,710 --> 00:10:33,390
export controls prevent it from selling EUV there.
美国的出口管制阻止了其向中国销售极紫外光刻机。

124
00:10:33,470 --> 00:10:36,270
It's a ban that started under the first Trump administration.
这项禁令始于特朗普政府第一任期。

125
00:10:36,510 --> 00:10:46,630
The Trump administration is very focused on ensuring that China does not get access to the most advanced tools and chips that are required to power AI.
特朗普政府非常关注确保中国无法获得用于推动人工智能的最先进工具和芯片。

126
00:10:46,990 --> 00:10:50,870
So without access to ASML's EUV machines, could China develop its own?
那么，在无法获得阿斯麦极紫外光刻机的情况下，中国能否自主研发？

127
00:10:51,110 --> 00:10:59,910
I feel like it's a real long shot that China could enter this space. But right now, China's really figuring out ways to take things like seven nanometer,
我觉得中国要进入这一领域几乎是不可能的。但目前中国正真正致力于寻找方法，将诸如七纳米制程等技术，

128
00:10:59,950 --> 00:11:04,110
the most advanced nodes that can be done without EUV, and figuring out ways to scale them.
这些无需极紫外光刻即可实现的最先进节点，进行规模化生产。

129
00:11:04,110 --> 00:11:09,230
And they've been able to do that successfully in some areas, like in smartphones and personal devices.
他们在某些领域已经成功实现，例如智能手机和个人设备。

130
00:11:09,590 --> 00:11:14,790
Still, export controls haven't stopped China from stockpiling ASML's less advanced machines.
尽管如此，出口管制并未阻止中国囤积阿斯麦的较旧款设备。

131
00:11:13,670 --> 00:11:21,120
At one point recently, u p to 49% of your business was in China. What happened there and what is that number at now?
最近一度，你业务的高达49%来自中国。当时发生了什么？现在这个数字是多少？

132
00:11:21,160 --> 00:11:28,720
We had a huge backlog in China because we got orders in 2022 at the peak of the market.
我们在中国积压了大量订单，因为2022年市场高峰期时接到了大量订单。

133
00:11:28,760 --> 00:11:37,200
And in 2023, 24, the rest of the world kind of went down. So basically we could use our capacity to fulfill this backlog.
2023年和2024年，世界其他地区整体下滑。因此，我们基本上可以利用现有产能来消化积压订单。

134
00:11:37,240 --> 00:11:41,960
End of 24, last quarter, the part of China in our business went down to 30%.
到2024年底，最后一个季度，中国业务占我们总业务的比例下降至30%。

135
00:11:43,400 --> 00:11:48,680
U.S. concern over advanced tech making its way to China has accelerated amidst the generative AI race.
美国对先进科技流向中国日益担忧，这一担忧在生成式AI竞赛中进一步加剧。

136
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:52,920
But that boom has also sent demand for chips and the machines that make them soaring.
但这一繁荣也推高了对芯片以及制造芯片的设备的需求。

137
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:57,320
And with it, chip stocks including ASML's, which hit an all time high in July.
伴随着这一趋势，包括阿斯麦在内的芯片股在7月创下历史新高。

138
00:11:57,880 --> 00:12:03,720
Still, it's declined some since as the chip industry faces uncertainties, chief among them Trump's tariffs.
然而，由于芯片行业面临不确定性，尤其是特朗普的关税政策，股价已有所回落。

139
00:12:04,040 --> 00:12:07,000
Any idea how tariffs are going to impact ASML?
你有没有想法，关税会对阿斯麦产生什么影响？

140
00:12:07,680 --> 00:12:09,400
Well the short answer is I don't know.
简短的回答是，我不知道。

141
00:12:09,440 --> 00:12:10,520
We we don't know.
我们不知道。

142
00:12:10,560 --> 00:12:13,600
And if anybody would know it could make a lot of money.
如果有人能知道，他可能赚到大钱。

143
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:14,400
But we don't.
但我们不知道。

144
00:12:15,320 --> 00:12:21,090
In its first quarter earnings reported last month. ASML missed on order expectations amid tariff uncertainty.
在上个月公布的首季度财报中，由于关税不确定性，阿斯麦的订单预期未达预期。

145
00:12:21,130 --> 00:12:28,530
I suspect ASML will come in and advocate for a very low to minimal to no tariff on their machines.
我怀疑阿斯麦会主张对其设备征收极低甚至零关税。

146
00:12:28,930 --> 00:12:38,930
The impact of tariffs is complicated by ASML's complex web of 800 global suppliers and the winding worldwide path. ASML's machines take before arriving in a fab.
阿斯麦复杂的全球供应商网络以及设备辗转全球的运输路径，使得关税的影响变得复杂。

147
00:12:39,330 --> 00:12:45,970
Each High NA machine is made up of four subsystems manufactured in Connecticut, Germany, the Netherlands and California.
每台高数值孔径设备由四个子系统组成，分别在康涅狄格州、德国、荷兰和加利福尼亚制造。

148
00:12:46,330 --> 00:12:51,010
Each module is shipped separately to ASML's headquarters in Veldhoven, where they are put together,
每个模块分别运送到阿斯麦位于费尔德霍芬的总部，在那里进行组装，

149
00:12:51,010 --> 00:12:54,930
tested, then disassembled again, bound for fabs in places like the U.S.
测试后再次拆解，运往美国等地的晶圆厂。

150
00:12:54,970 --> 00:12:56,530
or more frequently, Asia.
或更常见的是，运往亚洲。

151
00:12:57,370 --> 00:12:58,930
How do you ship something this massive?
你如何运输如此巨大的设备？

152
00:12:59,450 --> 00:13:09,010
Yeah, it takes about seven Boeing 747s to ship this whole thing, and it's about 25 to 30 trucks.
是的，运输整个设备大约需要七架波音747，以及25到30辆卡车。

153
00:13:17,990 --> 00:13:23,150
For years, Asia has made up more than 80% of ASML's business, but the U.S.
多年来，亚洲一直占阿斯麦业务的80%以上，但美国

154
00:13:23,190 --> 00:13:26,670
share, around 17% in 2024, is growing fast,
的份额在2024年约为17%，正在快速增长，

155
00:13:26,910 --> 00:13:33,950
especially as Intel builds new chip fabs in Ohio and Arizona. And TSMC is now in volume production in Arizona, too.
尤其是随着英特尔在俄亥俄州和亚利桑那州建设新的芯片晶圆厂。台积电如今也在亚利桑那州进入量产。

156
00:13:34,110 --> 00:13:36,470
So there's a lot of chip customers in the U.S.
因此，美国有大量芯片客户。

157
00:13:36,510 --> 00:13:40,270
So there is a, I would say, a good reason to have cheap manufacturing.
所以，我认为拥有廉价制造是有充分理由的。

158
00:13:40,430 --> 00:13:45,910
When we first got a look at EUV in 2022, ASML had about 32,000 employees.
2022年我们首次看到极紫外光刻技术时，阿斯麦大约有3.2万名员工。

159
00:13:46,030 --> 00:13:50,750
Today, that number has grown to 44,000, and 8,500 of them are in the US.
如今，这一数字已增长至4.4万人，其中8500人在美国。

160
00:13:50,790 --> 00:13:55,590
Like Eric Ma, who's been with ASML in San Jose, California, for 18 plus years.
就像埃里克·马，他在加利福尼亚州圣何塞的阿斯麦工作了18年以上。

161
00:13:55,630 --> 00:13:57,870
Have you gotten to see the High NA machines?
你见过高数值孔径设备吗？

162
00:13:57,910 --> 00:13:59,510
Yes. What is it like?
见过。感觉怎么样？

163
00:13:59,550 --> 00:14:00,470
Oh, it's huge.
哦，非常庞大。

164
00:14:01,110 --> 00:14:03,150
Of ASML's 60 global offices,
阿斯麦全球60个办公室中，

165
00:14:03,150 --> 00:14:10,230
18 of them are in the U.S., including a manufacturing site in Connecticut and R&D sites in San Diego and here in San Jose.
有18个位于美国，包括康涅狄格州的一处制造基地，以及圣迭戈和圣何塞的研发中心。

166
00:14:10,710 --> 00:14:13,750
We're here at ASML, Silicon Valley, California location.
我们现在位于阿斯麦，加利福尼亚州硅谷的办公地点。

167
00:14:13,750 --> 00:14:15,870
And behind me is a metrology machine.
我身后是一台量测设备。

168
00:14:15,950 --> 00:14:23,240
This one has 25 beams of electrons that are used to test the different microchips, to make sure that the yield is going to be good.
这台设备有25束电子束，用于测试不同的微芯片，以确保良率能够达标。

169
00:14:25,040 --> 00:14:32,160
For High NA in the U.S., it's likely that Arizona could be a major hub. Many of ASML's first High NA shipments went to Intel last year,
对于美国的高数值孔径技术，亚利桑那州很可能成为重要枢纽。去年，阿斯麦首批高数值孔径设备大多运往英特尔，

170
00:14:32,160 --> 00:14:36,960
and the struggling U.S.-based chipmaker is building a giant new chip fab in Chandler, Arizona.
而这家美国芯片制造商正于亚利桑那州钱德勒市建设一座巨大的新晶圆厂。

171
00:14:37,160 --> 00:14:48,040
Intel has been for many years a formidable partner for ASML, they were the first company to believe in EUV and the first company to work with us to develop EUV.
多年来，英特尔一直是阿斯麦的重要合作伙伴，他们是首家相信极紫外光刻技术的公司，也是首家与我们合作开发极紫外光刻技术的公司。

172
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:54,400
They have done the same on High NA, and I think that moving forward, the role of Intel for the U.S.
在高数值孔径领域，他们同样如此，我认为，未来英特尔对美国

173
00:14:54,680 --> 00:14:58,400
autonomy, independence on semiconductor is still very critical.
半导体自主与独立仍至关重要。

174
00:14:58,920 --> 00:15:07,920
But TSMC is far ahead of Intel in advancing chip nodes. We recently visited TSMC's new fab north of Phoenix, the most advanced chip fab on U.S.
但台积电在推进芯片制程节点方面远超英特尔。我们最近参观了台积电位于凤凰城以北的新晶圆厂，这是美国最先进的晶圆厂。

175
00:15:07,920 --> 00:15:14,040
soil. The need for High NA there will likely come soon, with ASML's original EUV machines in use now.
那里对高数值孔径设备的需求很可能很快就会到来，目前阿斯麦的原始极紫外光刻设备已在使用。

176
00:15:14,520 --> 00:15:23,340
In order to hook one up requires something over 2,000 electrical connections,
要安装一台设备，需要超过2000个电气连接，

177
00:15:23,340 --> 00:15:31,130
over two kilometers of cabling, 100,000 parts, 40,000 bolts.
超过两公里的电缆，10万多个零部件，4万多个螺栓。

178
00:15:31,490 --> 00:15:33,530
We're talking about massive.
我们谈论的是巨大的规模。

179
00:15:33,930 --> 00:15:35,970
With so many EUV machines in Arizona,
由于亚利桑那州将部署大量极紫外光刻设备，

180
00:15:36,010 --> 00:15:43,330
ASML is for the first time bringing a training facility to the US. Its only other training centers are in the Netherlands, Taiwan and Korea.
阿斯麦首次将培训中心带到美国。其仅有的其他培训中心位于荷兰、台湾和韩国。

181
00:15:43,730 --> 00:15:54,010
We're planning to open that in the next few months in Arizona, with the idea that we could train 1,200 people every year on EUV dpof.
我们计划在接下来的几个月内在亚利桑那州启动该项目，目标是每年培训1200人掌握EUV光刻技术。

182
00:15:55,250 --> 00:15:57,797
As chipmaking shows no signs of slowing in the U.S.
随着芯片制造在美国乃至全球均未显出放缓迹象，

183
00:15:57,797 --> 00:16:02,210
or elsewhere, ASML is already hard at work on its next generation machine, Hyper NA.
阿斯麦已全力投入下一代设备Hyper NA的研发。

184
00:16:02,330 --> 00:16:06,010
With an even larger NA that can print even smaller features.
其数值孔径更大，能够印刷更小的特征尺寸。

185
00:16:06,410 --> 00:16:08,690
I heard it could be up to $700 million.
我听说价格可能高达7亿美元。

186
00:16:08,690 --> 00:16:10,210
Do you have any price tag?
你有具体价格吗？

187
00:16:10,250 --> 00:16:13,770
Oh, it's way too early to mention the number, but typically price goes up.
哦，现在提具体数字还为时过早，但通常价格会随之上涨。

188
00:16:14,290 --> 00:16:16,650
So no, I don't think it's going to be that high.
所以不，我认为不会高到那个程度。

189
00:16:16,890 --> 00:16:22,340
Despite market headwinds, Fouquet told CNBC that customers will need Hyper NA within ten years.
尽管面临市场压力，傅恪礼告诉CNBC，客户将在十年内就需要Hyper NA。

190
00:16:22,780 --> 00:16:24,580
Anything you can tell us about Hyper NA?
你能透露一些关于Hyper NA的信息吗？

191
00:16:24,620 --> 00:16:26,300
How far away are we from seeing that?
我们距离看到它还有多远？

192
00:16:26,700 --> 00:16:30,860
For us, it's not necessarily a difficult product.
对我们而言，这并非一个必然难以实现的产品。

193
00:16:31,420 --> 00:16:33,820
We need our customers to need it as well.
我们的客户也需要它。

194
00:16:33,860 --> 00:16:42,180
And if you look at the roadmap of our customer, I think the need for Hyper NA will be somewhere between 2032 and 2035.
如果你看看我们客户的路线图，我认为对 Hyper NA 的需求将在 2032 年到 2035 年之间出现。

195
00:16:42,340 --> 00:16:51,860
But for now, ASML is focused on meeting demand for High NA. It plans to ship at least five more systems this year, ramping to a production capacity of 20 machines in a few years.
但目前，阿斯麦专注于满足 High NA 的需求。公司计划今年再交付至少五套系统，几年内将产能提升至每年 20 台。

196
00:16:52,340 --> 00:17:00,220
While this is a monopoly right here and today, in the era of AI, there will be new vehicles for building semiconductors.
虽然目前这是个垄断局面，但在 AI 时代，将出现新的半导体制造途径。

197
00:17:00,220 --> 00:17:06,820
And if I'm ASML, if I'm from any other company in this space, I'm being careful to make sure that I'm protecting my position, not just in the
如果我是阿斯麦，或者来自这个领域的任何其他公司，我都会谨慎行事，确保不仅保护好当前地位，

198
00:17:06,820 --> 00:17:08,300
near term, but in the long term as well.
也保护好长期地位。
